          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1778072188292_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Input: {{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_BALANCES_RESPONSE_FOR_DISPLAY.$output}}\nInsight_Response: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result}}\n\nYou are a specialized UI rendering assistant for dynamic table records. You\nmust adhere to the standard `oraInfoDisplay` Knowledge Base.\n\nYour task is to transform the provided input JSON into the following top-level\nblocks in this exact order:\n\n1. one `oraInfoDisplay` block\n2. zero or one `oraInsight` block for Explain, only when\n   `Insight_Response.showExplain` is true\n3. zero, one, two, or three insight-level `oraInsight` action blocks, based\n   only on `Insight_Response.showOpenActions` and\n   `Insight_Response.showReopenActions`\n4. one `oraComms` block\n\nDo not output anything else.\n\nThis node is render-only. It must not answer unrelated substance, personal\nquestions, or safety-sensitive questions. If unrelated or personal content is\npresent, do not respond to it. Render only the provided input according to this\nprompt. For self-harm, violence, abuse, or immediate-safety topics, follow\nplatform safety rules first and do not provide instructions or detailed\ncounseling.\n\n---\n\n# CRITICAL RULES\n\n- Do not output markdown.\n- Do not output explanations.\n- Do not output prose before or after the blocks.\n- Do not output code fences.\n- Do not output plain JSON objects by themselves.\n- Do not place actions inside `oraInfoDisplay`.\n- Do not place actions in an `\"actions\"` property.\n- Every visible value in `oraInfoDisplay` must come from the provided input\n  JSON or from an explicitly defined generic fallback in this prompt.\n- Do not infer, normalize, correct, or regenerate period names.\n- Do not change any period punctuation, spacing, casing, or month value.\n\n---\n\n# INPUT\n\n- Data: {{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_BALANCES_RESPONSE_FOR_DISPLAY.$output}}\n- Insight_Response: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result}}\n\n---\n\n# INSIGHT_RESPONSE STRUCTURE\n\n`Insight_Response` has the following structure:\n\n{\n  insightRecipientId,\n  ruleName,\n  categoryCode,\n  categoryCodeMeaning,\n  insightSummary,\n  statusCode,\n  statusMeaning,\n  showExplain,\n  showOpenActions,\n  showReopenActions\n}\n\nUse `Insight_Response` only for action visibility and action payload rules\ndescribed in this prompt.\n\n---\n\n# INPUT RULES\n\n- The input is a real JSON object.\n- The input may contain:\n  - `metadata`\n  - `summary`\n  - `table.columns`\n  - `table.rows`\n  - `actions`\n\n- Read values only from the input object.\n- Ignore the input `actions` array completely.\n- Do not render any action from the input.\n- Do not invent field names.\n- Do not hardcode column names.\n- Do not hardcode row field mappings.\n- Do not output values from examples, prior runs, memory, or unrelated tasks.\n- Do not substitute generic records when input data is available.\n- Do not output any row, column, title, description, subtitle, badge, status,\n  severity, or label that is not derived from the current input.\n- Do not alter period names. If the input says `Jan-16`, output `Jan-16`.\n\n---\n\n# COLUMN RENDERING RULES\n\nThe upstream node has already generated the final display labels and formatted\ncell values. This node is render-only except for typed numeric formatting of\namount-related, count-related, and percentage-related columns when explicitly\nallowed by this prompt.\n\nFor each object in input `table.columns`:\n- create exactly one output column in the same position.\n- use `table.columns[i].label` exactly as received when it is non-empty.\n- if `table.columns[i].label` is missing, null, or empty, use\n  `table.columns[i].key` exactly as received.\n- do not derive a label from the key when label is present.\n- do not title-case, split, normalize, translate, abbreviate, or reformat\n  labels.\n- do not append currency.\n- do not remove currency.\n- do not change period names.\n- infer numeric type only for amount-related, count-related, or\n  percentage-related columns when the values are numeric and the column is not\n  an identifier, code, date, period, currency, rate, flag, status, metadata,\n  debug, helper, or link field.\n- do not rebuild amount labels.\n\nIf the input column object explicitly contains `valueType` or `pattern`, copy\nthose properties exactly. The label must still remain exactly the input label\nor key fallback.\n\nIf the input column object does not contain `valueType` or `pattern`, output\nthe column header as the exact label string or key fallback string, except when\nall of the following are true:\n- the column is amount-related, count-related, or percentage-related by\n  semantic meaning from its label or key\n- the column is not an identifier, code, date, period, currency, rate, flag,\n  status, metadata, debug, helper, or link field\n- every non-empty value for that column in `table.rows` is numeric according to\n  the applicable numeric rules in this prompt\n\nWhen all of these conditions are true, output the column as a typed numeric\ncolumn object.\n\nFor amount-related numeric columns, use:\n\n{\n  \"label\": \"{Exact Input Label Or Key Fallback}\",\n  \"valueType\": \"number\",\n  \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n}\n\nFor count-related numeric columns, use:\n\n{\n  \"label\": \"{Exact Input Label Or Key Fallback}\",\n  \"valueType\": \"number\",\n  \"pattern\": \"0,0\"\n}\n\nFor percentage-related numeric columns, use:\n\n{\n  \"label\": \"{Exact Input Label Or Key Fallback}\",\n  \"valueType\": \"number\",\n  \"pattern\": \"0.0\"\n}\n\nDo not change the label text when creating the typed numeric column object.\nDo not append currency.\nDo not remove currency already present in the input label.\nDo not rebuild amount labels.\n\nNever create standalone currency columns.\nNever create checkbox columns.\nNever create action columns.\n\n---\n\n# NO-DATA FALLBACK RULES\n\n- If `table.columns` is missing, null, empty, or not an array, output an\n  `oraInfoDisplay` using `multiRecordWidget` with no columns and no rows.\n- If `table.rows` is missing, null, empty, or not an array, output the dynamic\n  columns from `table.columns` and an empty rows array.\n- Never fill missing data with sample rows.\n- Never fill missing columns with sample columns.\n\n---\n\n# ROOT CONFIGURATION\n\nThe root `oraInfoDisplay` must include:\n- `title`: an empty string.\n- `description`: use `summary.headline` directly if present and non-empty;\n  otherwise use `Details`.\n\nDo not generate or infer a title.\n\nDo not paraphrase `summary.headline`.\n\nDo not normalize period names in `summary.headline`.\n\n---\n\n# STRUCTURE RULES\n\n- Generate exactly one `oraInfoDisplay` using `multiRecordWidget`.\n- The widget must use the `multiRecordWidget` pattern only.\n- Treat the input as a JSON object containing:\n  - `table.columns`\n  - `table.rows`\n- Columns are dynamic and must be generated only from `table.columns`.\n- Rows are dynamic and must be generated only from `table.rows`.\n- Use only the columns provided in `table.columns`.\n- Preserve the column order exactly as received in `table.columns`.\n- Preserve the row order exactly as received in `table.rows`.\n- Do not add columns that are not present in `table.columns`.\n- Do not add rows that are not present in `table.rows`.\n\n---\n\n# DYNAMIC COLUMN RULES\n\nColumn labels are immutable.\n\nFor each object in `table.columns`, create exactly one column in the\n`multiRecordWidget`.\n\nUse this source for the visible column header:\n\n1. `table.columns[i].label` exactly as received, when non-empty\n2. `table.columns[i].key` exactly as received, only when label is missing,\n   null, or empty\n\nDo not display the key value when a non-empty label exists.\n\nDo not remove, rename, reorder, merge, transform, normalize, or regenerate\ncolumns from `table.columns`.\n\nDo not make period suffixes readable.\n\nDo not alter period punctuation or spacing.\n\nThis node must not decide which of those labels is correct. It must preserve\nthe upstream label exactly, including labels inside typed numeric column\nobjects.\n\n---\n\n# NUMERIC COLUMN RULES\n\nThis node may infer typed numeric columns only for:\n1. amount-related numeric fields\n2. count-related numeric fields\n3. percentage-related numeric fields\n\nA column is amount-related only when its label or key semantically represents a\nfinancial monetary amount, including balance measure fields, variance amount,\ndebit amount, credit amount, entered amount, accounted amount, transaction\namount, ledger amount, beginning balance, ending balance, period activity,\nperiod net balance, net balance, or similar monetary value.\n\nExpected amount-related balance fields may include, but are not limited to:\n- beginBalance\n- periodNetBalance\n- endingBalance\n- enteredBeginBalance\n- enteredPeriodNetBalance\n- enteredEndingBalance\n- accountedBeginBalance\n- accountedPeriodNetBalance\n- accountedEndingBalance\n- varianceAmount\n\nA column is count-related only when its label or key semantically represents a\ncount, number of records, number of rows, number of journals, number of lines,\nnumber of batches, number of accounts, occurrence count, transaction count,\njournal count, line count, batch count, record count, or similar counted\nquantity.\n\nA column is percentage-related only when its label or key semantically\nrepresents a percent or percentage measure, including variance percent,\nvariance percentage, percentage, percent, variance %, or similar percentage\nmeasure fields.\n\nExpected percentage-related fields may include, but are not limited to:\n- variancePercent\n- variancePercentage\n- percent\n- percentage\n\nA numeric field may include a source-provided suffix, period suffix,\ncomparison suffix, debit/credit variant, count variant, percentage variant, or\nother service-provided measure variant. Preserve the input column label exactly.\n\nNever infer a typed numeric column for:\n- identifiers\n- IDs\n- codes\n- account numbers\n- ledger IDs\n- journal IDs\n- batch IDs\n- line numbers\n- period names\n- accountingPeriod fields\n- dates\n- years\n- currency codes\n- rates\n- flags\n- statuses\n- ledger fields\n- COA segment fields\n- metadata\n- helper fields\n- debug fields\n- links\n\nUse a typed numeric column object only when every non-empty value for that\ncolumn in `table.rows` is numeric according to the applicable rule below.\n\nFor amount-related and count-related fields, a value is numeric when it is:\n- a JSON number, or\n- a string containing only a numeric value after trimming whitespace and\n  removing comma thousands separators\n\nFor percentage-related fields, a value is numeric when it is:\n- a JSON number, or\n- a string containing only a numeric value after trimming whitespace, removing\n  comma thousands separators, and removing one trailing percent sign\n\nNumeric strings may include:\n- a leading minus sign\n- decimal places\n- comma thousands separators\n\nPercentage strings may include:\n- a leading minus sign\n- decimal places\n- comma thousands separators\n- one trailing percent sign\n\nExamples of valid amount/count numeric values:\n- 12693630\n- 12693630.50\n- 12,693,630.50\n- -6455000.00\n- -6,455,000.00\n\nExamples of valid percentage numeric values:\n- 12.3\n- 12.3%\n- -5.0\n- -5.0%\n\n\nNull, missing, and empty values do not prevent an amount-related,\ncount-related, or percentage-related column from being typed as numeric. Their\nrow cells must be empty strings.\n\nFor inferred typed numeric amount columns, use this column pattern:\n\n{\n  \"label\": \"{Exact Input Label Or Key Fallback}\",\n  \"valueType\": \"number\",\n  \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n}\n\nFor inferred typed numeric count columns, use this column pattern:\n\n{\n  \"label\": \"{Exact Input Label Or Key Fallback}\",\n  \"valueType\": \"number\",\n  \"pattern\": \"0,0\"\n}\n\nFor inferred typed numeric percentage columns, use this column pattern:\n\n{\n  \"label\": \"{Exact Input Label Or Key Fallback}\",\n  \"valueType\": \"number\",\n  \"pattern\": \"0.0\"\n}\n\nThe label must remain exactly the input `table.columns[i].label` when non-empty,\nor exactly the input `table.columns[i].key` fallback when label is missing,\nnull, or empty.\n\n---\n\n# DYNAMIC ROW MAPPING RULES\n\n- Each object in `table.rows` must map to exactly one row.\n- For each generated column, get the cell value from the current row using the\n  matching column `key`.\n- Apply this lookup generically for every column object in `table.columns`.\n- Do not hardcode any specific key names.\n- If a row does not contain the column `key`, omit that cell value.\n- If a row value is missing, null, or empty, omit that cell value.\n- Do not invent values.\n- Do not transform values except for inferred typed numeric amount, count, and\n  percentage columns.\n- Do not abbreviate values.\n- Do not convert numbers except for inferred typed numeric amount, count, and\n  percentage columns.\n- Do not convert dates.\n- Do not add badges unless the badge structure is explicitly present in the\n  input value.\n- Do not add severity styling unless severity styling is explicitly present in\n  the input value.\n- Do not add status styling unless status styling is explicitly present in the\n  input value.\n- preserve visible values exactly as received\n- do not convert formatted numeric strings into numbers\n- do not remove thousands separators\n- do not remove decimal places\n- Do not remove or append currency.\n- Do not alter period names in any cell value.\n- Use the value exactly as received from\n  `table.rows[rowIndex][column.key]`, except for inferred typed numeric amount,\n  count, and percentage columns where the numeric value must be emitted as a\n  JSON number.\n\n---\n\n# OUTPUT STRUCTURE EXAMPLE\n\nUse this structure. The example values are placeholders only and must not be\ncopied into the output.\n\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"{wrapper-key}\">\n{\n  \"title\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"{summary.headline or Details}\",\n  \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cols\": [\n      \"{Column Label 1}\",\n      {\n        \"label\": \"{Amount Numeric Column Label 2}\",\n        \"valueType\": \"number\",\n        \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"{Count Numeric Column Label 3}\",\n        \"valueType\": \"number\",\n        \"pattern\": \"0,0\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"{Percentage Numeric Column Label 4}\",\n        \"valueType\": \"number\",\n        \"pattern\": \"0.0\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"rows\": [\n      {\n        \"cells\": [\n          \"{cellValue1}\",\n          \"{cellValue2}\",\n          \"{cellValue3}\",\n          \"{cellValue4}\"\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\n---\n\n# VALIDATION RULES BEFORE OUTPUT\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that every column header came from\n`table.columns[*].label` or the matching `table.columns[*].key` fallback.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that every row cell came from the\ncurrent row object using the matching column `key`.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that the number of output rows equals\nthe number of objects in `table.rows`.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that no sample, demo, placeholder,\nalert, status, or unrelated record was introduced.\n\nIf a value cannot be traced to the current input JSON, remove it.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify byte-for-byte label preservation,\nincluding labels inside typed numeric column objects:\n\nFor every output column at index i:\n- if input `table.columns[i].label` is non-empty, the visible output header\n  must exactly equal input `table.columns[i].label`.\n- otherwise, the visible output header must exactly equal\n  input `table.columns[i].key`.\n\nIf the output header differs by even one character, replace it with the exact\ninput value.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that typed numeric columns were\ninferred only for amount-related, count-related, or percentage-related fields.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that amount-related typed numeric\ncolumns use pattern \"0,0.00\".\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that count-related typed numeric\ncolumns use pattern \"0,0\".\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that percentage-related typed numeric\ncolumns use pattern \"0.0\".\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that no identifier, code, date,\nperiod, currency, rate, flag, status, ledger field, COA segment field,\nmetadata, debug, helper, or link field was typed as numeric.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that cells for inferred typed numeric\namount, count, and percentage columns are JSON numbers when valid and\nnon-empty, and empty strings otherwise.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that percentage cells had at most one\ntrailing percent sign removed before being emitted as JSON numbers.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that any amount or count cell\ncontaining currency text, currency symbols, period names, words, or mixed text\nremains a string and is not typed as numeric.\n\nBefore producing the final output, verify that all non-typed column values are\npreserved exactly as received.\n\n- Do not change hyphenated periods to spaced periods.\n- Do not substitute one month for another.\n\n---\n\n# ACTION RULES\n\n- Do not include row actions.\n- Do not include cell actions.\n- Do not include actions inside `oraInfoDisplay`.\n- After the closing `oraInfoDisplay`, output `oraInsight` blocks only when the\n  conditions in TOP-LEVEL EXPLAIN ACTION BLOCK and INSIGHT-LEVEL ACTION BLOCK\n  are satisfied.\n- Follow TOP-LEVEL EXPLAIN ACTION BLOCK and INSIGHT-LEVEL ACTION BLOCK rules\n  for generating actions.\n\n---\n\n# TOP-LEVEL EXPLAIN ACTION BLOCK\n\nAfter the closing `oraInfoDisplay`, output 1 `<oraInsight>` block only when\n`Insight_Response.showExplain` is true.\n\nWhen `Insight_Response.showExplain` is false, missing, null, or not true, do\nnot output the Explain `<oraInsight>` block.\n\nWhen included, the `<oraInsight>` block must follow this shape:\n\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Explain\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Explain\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": `ora.Invoke(\"openClrAccBalInsight\", {\n\"actionCode\": \"openClrAccBalInsight\",\n\"secActionCode\": \"explain\",\n\"workflow\": \"ORA_VARIANCE_ANALYSIS\",\n\"rowData\" : {\n\"insightRecipientId\" :\n{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.insightId || \"300100653755355\"}}\n} } )`\n}\n</oraInsight>\n\n---\n\n# INSIGHT-LEVEL ACTION BLOCK\n\nAfter the existing display blocks, add insight-level `oraInsight` actions\nbased only on `Insight_Response.showOpenActions` and\n`Insight_Response.showReopenActions`.\n\nWhen `Insight_Response.showOpenActions` is true, add exactly two `oraInsight`\nactions: Mark as Reviewed and Dismiss.\n\nPreserve the `followUpCommand` values exactly as shown below. Do not add any\nadditional `oraInsight` blocks for open actions.\n\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Mark as Reviewed\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Mark as Reviewed\",\n  \"workflow\": \"ORA_VARIANCE_ANALYSIS\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"markAsReviewed\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\" : \\\"markAsReviewed\\\", \\\"rowData\\\" : {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result}} })\"\n}\n</oraInsight>\n\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Dismiss\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Dismiss\",\n  \"workflow\": \"ORA_VARIANCE_ANALYSIS\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"dismiss\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\" : \\\"dismiss\\\", \\\"rowData\\\" : {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result}} })\"\n}\n</oraInsight>\n\nWhen `Insight_Response.showReopenActions` is true, add exactly one\n`oraInsight` action: Reopen.\n\nPreserve the `followUpCommand` value exactly as shown below. Do not add any\nadditional `oraInsight` blocks for reopen action.\n\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Reopen\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Reopen\",\n  \"workflow\": \"ORA_VARIANCE_ANALYSIS\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"reopenInsight\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\" : \\\"reopenInsight\\\", \\\"rowData\\\" : {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result}} })\"\n}\n</oraInsight>\n\nWhen `Insight_Response.showOpenActions` is false, missing, null, or not true,\ndo not add Mark as Reviewed or Dismiss actions.\n\nWhen `Insight_Response.showReopenActions` is false, missing, null, or not\ntrue, do not add the Reopen action.\n\n---\n\n# COMMUNICATION ACTION LOGIC\n\nGenerate exactly one email communication `oraComms` block after the generated\naction blocks.\n\n`title` should be:\n`{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result.ruleName}}`\n\n`shortDescription` should be:\n`{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result.insightSummary}}`\n\nThe email body must include:\n\n1. The generated Summary line exactly as rendered at the top of the UI output.\n2. The same `oraInfoDisplay` block rendered in the UI output.\n\nEmail rendering rules:\n- Paste the same UI data into the email body without changing its meaning.\n- Preserve the order used in the UI output.\n- Render each `oraInfoDisplay` as a readable HTML section.\n- For each `oraInfoDisplay`, include its `title` and `description` as-is.\n- Render `properties.cols` as the HTML table header when present.\n- Render `properties.rows` as the HTML table body when present.\n- Preserve column order exactly as provided.\n- Preserve row order exactly as provided.\n- Preserve field names and values exactly as provided, except for inferred typed\n  numeric amount, count, and percentage columns where the UI value is the JSON\n  numeric value.\n- If a value is empty or null, leave the table cell empty.\n- Do not paraphrase, summarize, rename, translate, or normalize values.\n- Do not add conclusions or commentary.\n- Use HTML `<b>` tags only for headers and sub-headers.\n- Use simple HTML table structure with inline-safe formatting.\n- Use `{{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}` exactly for the sender\n  name.\n- For email tables, reuse the same generated `oraInfoDisplay` `properties.cols`\n  and `properties.rows` values. Do not regenerate labels or cells for email.\n- Email table headers must exactly match the visible UI table headers.\n- Email table cells must exactly match the visible UI table cells.\n- Do not normalize, paraphrase, rename, translate, or reformat period names in\n  email content.\n\n---\n\n# EMAIL METADATA\n\nThe `oraComms` block must contain this metadata shape:\n\n<oraComms>\n{\n  \"title\": `{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result.ruleName}}`,\n  \"shortDescription\": `{{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result.insightSummary}}`,\n  \"actionText\": \"Send Email\",\n  \"type\": \"email\",\n  \"priority\": true,\n  \"content\": \"Follow SAMPLE EMAIL STRUCTURE as wrapper and generate email content from the Summary line and the rendered oraInfoDisplay. Do not paraphrase, summarize, rename, translate, normalize, or alter the data. Preserve the UI output order. Include the Summary line exactly as rendered. For every oraInfoDisplay from the email body requirements, render the title and description as-is, then render properties.cols as the HTML table header and properties.rows as the HTML table body. Preserve all column order, row order, field names, labels, period names, and values exactly. If a value is empty or null, leave it empty.\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"email\",\n      \"title\": \"email address\",\n      \"defaultValue\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"subject\",\n      \"title\": \"Generate a short subject based on the rendered Summary line and financial data. Make it concise.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n</oraComms>\n\n---\n\n# SAMPLE EMAIL STRUCTURE\n\n<p>Hi Team,</p>\n\n<p>Please review the following summary:</p>\n<br/>\n{{Render oraInfoDisplay block as an HTML section with title, description, and\ntable.\nUse <b> tags only for section headers and sub-headers.\nUse <br/> after each table.\nUse <table border=\\\"1\\\" cellpadding=\\\"6\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\"\nstyle=\\\"border-collapse: collapse; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\nfont-size: 13px; width: 100%;\\\"> for tables.}}\n<br/>\nBest Regards<br/>\n{{$context.$app.$OraUserContext.fullName}}\n\n---\n\n# CONSTRAINTS\n\n- Do not add checkbox columns.\n- Do not add action columns.\n- Do not add extra columns.\n- Do not invent values.\n- Omit missing/null/empty mapped values unless explicitly defined.\n- Use only `multiRecordWidget`.\n- Do not infer, correct, or normalize period names.\n- Do not substitute one period for another.\n\n---\n\n# OUTPUT RULES\n\n- Output only the final `oraInfoDisplay`, followed by only the conditional\n  `oraInsight` blocks allowed by this prompt, followed by exactly one\n  `oraComms` block.\n- No markdown.\n- No explanations.\n- No extra text.\n- If any table value is not available in the input JSON, omit it rather than\n  replacing it with example data."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "id": "1779964287605",
          "code": "DETERMINE_INSIGHT_FLOW_TYPE",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Determine Insight Flow Type",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const parseFilterFromPayload = (payload) => {\n  const filter = getFilterFromPayload(payload);\n  return filter ? parseFilter(filter) : {};\n};\n\n// Fetches filter string from the Balances AV query\nconst getFilterFromPayload = (payload) => {\n  const analyticViews = payload?.analyticViews;\n\n  if (!analyticViews || typeof analyticViews !== \"object\") {\n    return \"\";\n  }\n\n  const firstAnalyticView = Object.values(analyticViews)[0];\n\n  return typeof firstAnalyticView?.filter === \"string\"\n    ? firstAnalyticView.filter\n    : \"\";\n};\n\nconst parseFilter = (filter) => {\n  const conditions = splitByLogicalAnd(filter);\n  const result = {};\n\n  for (const condition of conditions) {\n    let parsedCondition;\n\n    try {\n      parsedCondition = parseCondition(condition);\n    } catch (error) {\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    const {\n      dimension,\n      attribute,\n      operator,\n      value,\n      original,\n      expression\n    } = parsedCondition;\n\n    result[dimension] ??= {};\n\n    result[dimension][attribute] = {\n      operator,\n      value,\n      original,\n      expression\n    };\n  }\n\n  return result;\n};\n\n// Splits by AND, but ignores AND inside quotes or parentheses\nconst splitByLogicalAnd = (filter) => {\n  const conditions = [];\n\n  let current = \"\";\n  let insideQuote = false;\n  let parenthesesDepth = 0;\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < filter.length; i++) {\n    const char = filter[i];\n\n    if (char === \"'\") {\n      insideQuote = !insideQuote;\n      current += char;\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    if (!insideQuote) {\n      if (char === \"(\") {\n        parenthesesDepth++;\n      } else if (char === \")\") {\n        parenthesesDepth--;\n      }\n\n      const remaining = filter.slice(i);\n      const andMatch = remaining.match(/^\\s+\\band\\b\\s+/i);\n\n      if (parenthesesDepth === 0 && andMatch) {\n        conditions.push(current.trim());\n        current = \"\";\n\n        i += andMatch[0].length - 1;\n        continue;\n      }\n    }\n\n    current += char;\n  }\n\n  if (current.trim()) {\n    conditions.push(current.trim());\n  }\n\n  return conditions;\n};\n\n// Parses one condition\nconst parseCondition = (condition) => {\n  const original = condition.trim();\n\n  const operatorMatch = findOperator(original);\n\n  if (!operatorMatch) {\n    throw new Error(`Unsupported condition: ${condition}`);\n  }\n\n  const operator = normalizeOperator(operatorMatch.operator);\n\n  const leftSide = original.slice(0, operatorMatch.index).trim();\n\n  const rightSide = original\n    .slice(operatorMatch.index + operatorMatch.raw.length)\n    .trim();\n\n  const { dimension, attribute } = parseLeftSide(leftSide);\n\n  return {\n    dimension,\n    attribute,\n    operator,\n    value: parseValue(operator, rightSide),\n    original,\n    expression: `${operator} ${rightSide}`\n  };\n};\n\n// Finds supported operators\nconst findOperator = (condition) => {\n  const match = condition.match(\n    /\\s+(not\\s+in|in)\\s*(?=\\()|\\s+(not\\s+in|in)\\s+|\\s*(>=|<=|!=|>|<|=)\\s*/i\n  );\n\n  if (!match) {\n    return null;\n  }\n\n  return {\n    index: match.index,\n    raw: match[0],\n    operator: match[1] || match[2] || match[3]\n  };\n};\n\n// Normalizes operator casing\nconst normalizeOperator = (operator) => {\n  return operator\n    .trim()\n    .replace(/\\s+/g, \" \")\n    .toUpperCase();\n};\n\n// Splits left side into dimension and attribute\nconst parseLeftSide = (leftSide) => {\n  const dotIndex = leftSide.indexOf(\".\");\n\n  if (dotIndex === -1) {\n    throw new Error(`Invalid condition left side: ${leftSide}`);\n  }\n\n  return {\n    dimension: leftSide.slice(0, dotIndex).trim(),\n    attribute: leftSide.slice(dotIndex + 1).trim()\n  };\n};\n\n// Parses right-side value\nconst parseValue = (operator, rawValue) => {\n  if (operator === \"IN\" || operator === \"NOT IN\") {\n    return parseListValue(rawValue);\n  }\n\n  return stripOuterQuotes(rawValue);\n};\n\n// Parses values inside IN (...)\nconst parseListValue = (rawValue) => {\n  const trimmed = rawValue.trim();\n\n  if (!trimmed.startsWith(\"(\") || !trimmed.endsWith(\")\")) {\n    throw new Error(`Invalid list value: ${rawValue}`);\n  }\n\n  const innerValue = trimmed.slice(1, -1);\n  const parts = splitCommaSeparatedValues(innerValue);\n\n  return parts.map(stripOuterQuotes);\n};\n\n// Splits comma-separated values\nconst splitCommaSeparatedValues = (value) => {\n  const result = [];\n\n  let current = \"\";\n  let insideQuote = false;\n\n  for (let i = 0; i < value.length; i++) {\n    const char = value[i];\n\n    if (char === \"'\") {\n      insideQuote = !insideQuote;\n      current += char;\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    if (char === \",\" && !insideQuote) {\n      result.push(current.trim());\n      current = \"\";\n      continue;\n    }\n\n    current += char;\n  }\n\n  if (current.trim()) {\n    result.push(current.trim());\n  }\n\n  return result;\n};\n\n// Removes surrounding quotes\nconst stripOuterQuotes = (value) => {\n  const trimmed = String(value).trim();\n\n  if (trimmed.startsWith(\"'\") && trimmed.endsWith(\"'\")) {\n    return trimmed.slice(1, -1);\n  }\n\n  return trimmed;\n};\n\n// Extract accountingPeriod.$memberName values\nconst getAccountingPeriodMemberNames = (payload) => {\n  const parsed = parseFilterFromPayload(payload);\n\n  const value = parsed?.accountingPeriod?.$memberName?.value;\n\n  if (!value) {\n    return [];\n  }\n\n  return Array.isArray(value) ? value : [value];\n};\n\n// Usage\nlet balancesAVRequest = $context.$nodes.PROCESS_RESOLVED_INSIGHT_CRITERIA.$output.result;\n\nif (typeof balancesAVRequest === \"string\") {\n  balancesAVRequest = JSON.parse(balancesAVRequest);\n}\n\nlet periodNames = [];\nlet classification = \"ORA_OTHERS\";\n\ntry {\n  periodNames = getAccountingPeriodMemberNames(balancesAVRequest) || [];\n  classification = periodNames.length === 2 ? \"ORA_VARIANCE\" : \"ORA_OTHERS\";\n} catch (e) {\n  return {\n    classification: \"ORA_OTHERS\",\n    periodNames: [],\n    error: e.message\n  };\n}\n\nreturn {\n  classification,\n  periodNames\n};"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11342.5,
            "y": 10756
          },
          "outcomes": {
