        {
          "id": "1779965352698",
          "code": "GENERATE_EXPLANATION_FOR_INSIGHT",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Explanation For Insight",
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5408.5,
            "y": 23722
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779240670702_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1779240670702_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Oracle `oraInfoDisplay` and `oraInsight` output.\n\nYour task is to return, in this exact order:\n1. One Summary line before all `oraInfoDisplay` block(s), generated using `SUMMARY RULES`\n2. One summary `oraInfoDisplay` block\n3. The existing display blocks exactly as is, only when each output is non-null:\n   {{$context.$nodes.DISPLAY_JOURNAL_SOURCE_SUMMARY_DATA.$output}}\n   {{$context.$nodes.DISPLAY_JOURNAL_SOURCE_DETAILS.$output}}\n4. Exactly two `oraInsight` action blocks.\n\nDo not ask questions.\nDo not include markdown.\nDo not include explanatory text outside the required blocks.\nDo not change, escape, summarize, or reformat the existing display blocks\nfrom the two display-node outputs.\n\nSUMMARY `oraInfoDisplay` BLOCK\n\nReturn this block first:\n\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"journal-summary\">\n{\n  \"title\": \"Summary\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cols\": [],\n    \"rows\": []\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\nSUMMARY RULES:\n- Write a Reasoning Summary.\n- Generate a Root Cause Analysis narrative style.\n- Do not prefix the output with \"Summary:\", \"Reasoning:\", \"Explanation:\", \"RCA:\", or any other label.\n- Do not use bullets, markdown, headings, or JSON.\n- Identify the primary driver using `$Primary Data`.\n  - Explain why it is the primary driver.\n  - Support the statement with specific facts, amounts, currency, source/category, status, and exception indicators from the data.\n- Identify concentration or distribution using `$Secondary Data`.\n  - Support the primary driver statement with matching fields and related details from `$Secondary Data`.\n  - Mention relevant amounts, currency, status, source/category, and any. exception or status indicators.\n- Group the evidence into a business-friendly financial summary.\n  - Mention key matching fields.\n  - Mention amounts, currency, status, source/category, and exceptions when available.\n  - Do not mention IDs or rule names.\n  - Do not invent missing facts.\n  - If no exception is shown in the data, say no exception is indicated only when the data supports it.\n\nSUMMARY FORMATTING RULES:\n- Format monetary amounts in the Summary line as full numbers with thousands\n  separators.\n- Do not compact monetary amounts using K, M, B, T, or similar suffixes.\n- Preserve the minus sign when a source monetary amount is negative.\n- Use the currency code from the source data when available.\n- Do not use currency symbols.\n- Do not show Dr or Cr in the Summary line.\n- Format percentage values with exactly one decimal place followed by `%`.\n- Round percentage values using standard decimal rounding.\n- Do not show more than one digit after the decimal point for percentage\n  values.\n\n- Before responding, check that the output:\n  - does not start with \"Summary:\"\n  - contains only the summary narrative\n  - formats monetary amounts with thousands separators\n  - does not use compact amount notation\n  - formats percentage values with exactly one decimal place\n- Use Data:\n  - Primary: {{$context.$variables.JournalsFromBalancesAVResponse}} and {{$context.$nodes.DISPLAY_JOURNAL_SOURCE_SUMMARY_DATA.$output}}\n  - Secondary: {{$context.$variables.JournalsBVfromJournalsAVResponse}} and {{$context.$nodes.DISPLAY_JOURNAL_SOURCE_DETAILS.$output}}\n\nEXISTING DISPLAY BLOCKS\n\nAfter the summary `oraInfoDisplay` block, output the following content exactly\nas returned by the workflow nodes:\n\n{{$context.$nodes.DISPLAY_JOURNAL_SOURCE_SUMMARY_DATA.$output}} (if not null, else ignore)\n{{$context.$nodes.DISPLAY_JOURNAL_SOURCE_DETAILS.$output}} (if not null, else ignore)\n\nACTION LOGIC\n\nAfter the existing display blocks, add exactly two `oraInsight` actions.\n\nPreserve the `followUpCommand` values exactly as shown below. Do not add any additional `oraInsight` blocks.\n\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Mark as Reviewed\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Mark as Reviewed\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"markAsReviewed\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\" : \\\"markAsReviewed\\\", \\\"rowData\\\" : {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result}} })\"\n}\n</oraInsight>\n\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"Dismiss\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Dismiss\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"dismiss\\\", {\\\"actionCode\\\" : \\\"dismiss\\\", \\\"rowData\\\" : {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_INSIGHT_DETAILS.$output.result}} })\"\n}\n</oraInsight>\n\nFINAL VALIDATION\n\nBefore returning the final output:\n- Confirm the summary line at start before `oraInfoDisplay` blocks\n- Confirm the first block is exactly one `oraInfoDisplay` block with\n  `key=\"journal-summary\"`.\n- Confirm the two display-node outputs are included as-is.\n- Confirm exactly two `oraInsight` blocks are included\n- Confirm no markdown, explanations, or extra text are included."
            }
          ],
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "enableActions": true,
              "enablePowerPoints": false
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "1780943823217",
          "code": "PREPARE_JOURNALS_AV_PAYLOAD",
          "type": "CODE",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Prepare Journals AV Payload",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let bossQ =  JSON.parse( $context.$nodes.RESOLVE_FILTER_PERIODS_FOR_INSIGHT.$output || '');\nlet queries = [];\n\nif(typeof bossQ == \"string\"){\n    bossQ = JSON.parse(bossQ);\n}\n\nqueries.push(bossQ);\n\nlet payload = {\n    \"rowLimit\": 25,\n    \"ledgerId\": $context.$nodes.PARSE_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.ledgerId,\n    \"includeData\":true,\n    \"varianceColumn\": \"accountingPeriod.$memberName\",\n    \"expandAggregateDataByOneLevel\": true,\n    \"useCase\": \"LedgerInsights\",\n    \"expandBasedOnAccountType\": true,\n    \"queries\": queries\n};\n\npayload;"
          },
          "diagram": {
