        {
          "id": "1779964925896",
          "code": "DISPLAY_JOURNAL_SOURCE_SUMMARY_DATA",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Journal Source Summary Data",
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 Mini (Premium)",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelProperties": {
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              }
            },
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 5770,
            "y": 23465
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779965352698"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779229401344_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for journal source contribution summaries.\n\nYou must adhere to the standard `oraInfoDisplay` Knowledge Base.\n\nInputs\n\nJournals: {{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_JOURNAL_SOURCE_SUMMARY.$output.result}}\n\ncurrencyCode: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.currencyCode}}\n\nDirective\n\nTransform the provided ranked journal source contributor JSON array into one valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using the `multiRecordWidget` pattern.\n\nRoot Configuration\n\n- `title`: `Top Journal Source Contributors`\n- `description`: No description, leave it empty.\n- `patternId`: `multiRecordWidget`\n\nData Rules\n\n- Treat `Journals` as a JSON array.\n- Preserve the input rank order exactly.\n- Do not recalculate, infer, regroup, filter, or resort the data.\n- Do not include row actions.\n- If `Journals` is missing, null, empty, or not an array, return the same widget with the configured columns and no rows.\n\nColumns\n\nUse exactly these four columns in this order:\n\n1. `Rank`\n\n2. `Journal Source`\n\n3. Amount column:\n   - If `currencyCode` has exactly one valid non-empty currency value, use this numeric column object:\n\n     {\n       \"label\": \"Net Accounted Amount ({currencyCode})\",\n       \"valueType\": \"number\",\n       \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n     }\n\n   - If `currencyCode` is missing, empty, or invalid, use this numeric column object:\n\n     {\n       \"label\": \"Net Accounted Amount\",\n       \"valueType\": \"number\",\n       \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n     }\n\n4. `Contribution %`\n\nRow Mapping\n\nFor each row in `Journals`:\n\n1. `rows[].cells[0]`: map `rank`\n2. `rows[].cells[1]`: map `journalSource`\n3. `rows[].cells[2]`: map `netAccountedAmount`\n4. `rows[].cells[3]`: map `contributionPercentage`\n\nIf a mapped field is missing, null, or blank, display an empty string for that cell.\n\nNumeric Cell Rules\n\n- For `netAccountedAmount`, output non-empty valid numeric values as JSON numbers, not strings.\n- Remove comma thousands separators before output.\n- Do not quote numeric `netAccountedAmount` cell values.\n- Use an empty string for null, missing, empty, or non-numeric `netAccountedAmount` values.\n- For the typed amount column, output only the numeric amount.\n- Do not append currency codes to numeric amount cell values.\n- Rely on the numeric column `pattern` for display formatting.\n- Preserve the minus sign when `netAccountedAmount` is negative.\n- Do not compact `netAccountedAmount` using K, M, B, T, or similar suffixes.\n- Do not repeat the currency code inside amount cells.\n\nPercentage Formatting Rules\n\n- Format `contributionPercentage` with exactly one decimal place followed by `%`.\n- Round `contributionPercentage` using standard decimal rounding.\n- Do not show more than one digit after the decimal point for percentage values.\n- If `contributionPercentage` is missing, null, blank, or non-numeric, display an empty string.\n\nExclusion Rules\n\n- Do not include columns for `accountedDebit`, `accountedCredit`, `absoluteNetAccountedAmount`, or `cumulativeContributionPercentage`.\n\nOutput Rules\n\n- Return only the `oraInfoDisplay` XML block.\n- Do not include markdown, explanation, commentary, or text outside the XML.\n- Do not add fields, columns, rows, actions, summaries, or behavior beyond what is explicitly requested."
            }
          ],
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "1779965277198",
