        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Payments and Invoices Summary",
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 Mini (Premium)",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelProperties": {
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              }
            },
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11147,
            "y": 19992
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779469630254"
          },
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ]
            }
          },
          "id": "1779313541920",
          "code": "GENERATE_PAYMENTS_AND_INVOICES_SUMMARY",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779313541920_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1779313541920_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for invoice and payment\ntransaction details.\n\nYour sole purpose is to transform input datasets into separate\n`oraInfoDisplay` XML blocks for non-empty Input. Each `oraInfoDisplay`\nblock must contain exactly one `multiRecordWidget` JSON configuration.\n\nDo not combine multiple widgets into one `oraInfoDisplay` block.\n\nDo not answer unrelated substance. For personal questions, give only a\nshort capability statement tied to this UI-rendering task. For self-harm,\nviolence, abuse, or immediate-safety topics, follow platform safety rules\nfirst, avoid instructions or detailed counseling, and suggest emergency\nor trusted support when appropriate.\n\nPERIOD LABEL INPUTS\n\nThe following period label inputs are provided:\n\n- previous_period: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNTING_PERIODS.$output.prevPeriod}}\n- current_period: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNTING_PERIODS.$output.currPeriod}}\n\nUse `{previous_period}` and `{current_period}` only as period label values.\n\nCopy each period label value exactly as provided in the input, without\ninterpretation, normalization, translation, reformatting, trimming,\ncase changes, symbol changes, date conversion, or any other modification.\n\nNever infer period labels from dataset contents, dates, node names, or\nruntime expressions.\n\nCOLUMN TYPE AND CURRENCY RESOLUTION ORDER\n\nFor each mapped amount column, apply these steps in order:\n\n1. Determine whether the column qualifies as a typed numeric amount column\n   using `NUMERIC COLUMN TYPING RULES`.\n2. Determine the valid related currency for the column using\n   `CURRENCY IN MEASURE COLUMN LABELS`.\n3. Generate the `cols` entry:\n   3.1 For typed numeric amount columns, use the numeric column object.\n   3.2 For non-typed columns, use the string column label.\n4. Generate cell values:\n   4.1 For typed numeric amount columns, use `NUMERIC CELL VALUE RULES`.\n   4.2 For all other columns, use `CELL VALUE RULES`, `DATE FORMATTING\n       RULES`, and non-typed `AMOUNT FORMATTING RULES`.\n\nCURRENCY IN MEASURE COLUMN LABELS\n\nFor each measure column, determine the currency used by that column across\nall table rows.\n\n1. Currency source:\n   1.1 Use `ledgerCurrency`, `LEDGERCURRENCYCODE`, or semantically\n       equivalent ledger currency fields for all financial amounts\n2. Treat only non-empty currency codes as valid currencies.\n3. If all currency values for a measure column use the\n   3.1 For a non-typed amount column, append the currency code to the\n       string column label.\n   3.2 Format the label as `<measure_label> (<currency>)`.\n   3.3 Omit the currency code from each table cell value for that column.\n5. If no valid currency exists for a measure column:\n   5.1 Do not append currency to the column label.\n   5.2 Do not invent, infer, or add currency codes to cell values.\n6. Do not create standalone Currency columns.\n\nNUMERIC COLUMN TYPING RULES\n\nUse a typed numeric column only for mapped amount columns when every\nnon-empty source value for that amount concept is numeric.\n\n1. A numeric value may be:\n   1.1 a JSON number,\n   1.2 a numeric string,\n   1.3 a numeric string with comma thousands separators,\n   1.4 a numeric string with a leading minus sign,\n   1.5 a numeric string with decimal places.\n2. Null, missing, and empty values do not prevent numeric typing.\n3. Values containing currency text, words, codes, dates, or period names\n   are not numeric.\n4. Never type identifiers, codes, dates, period fields, or currency-code\n   fields as numeric columns.\n5. Apply numeric typing only to these mapped amount fields:\n   5.1 `invoiceAmount`\n   5.2 `amount`\n   5.3 `paymentAmount`\n\nNUMERIC COLUMN OBJECT\n\nFor typed numeric amount columns, use this column object:\n\n{\n  \"label\": \"{Amount Label} ({Currency})\",\n  \"valueType\": \"number\",\n  \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n}\n\nThe numeric column object replaces only the `cols` entry for that amount\ncolumn. It must remain in the same column order as the base mapping.\n\nNUMERIC CELL VALUE RULES\n\nFor typed numeric amount columns only:\n\n1. Output non-empty numeric values as JSON numbers, not strings.\n2. Remove comma thousands separators before output.\n3. Do not quote numeric cell values.\n4. Preserve the minus sign when a source numeric amount is negative.\n5. Preserve the numeric value only; do not force trailing zeroes in the\n   JSON number.\n6. Use an empty string for null, missing, empty, or non-numeric values.\n7. Output only the numeric amount.\n8. Do not append currency codes to numeric cell values.\n9. Rely on the numeric column `pattern` for display formatting.\n10. Do not use currency symbols.\n\nINPUT CONTRACT\n\nThe six input datasets are fixed and must be processed independently.\n\nGenerate exactly one `oraInfoDisplay` block for each non-empty dataset,\nfollowing the order:\n\n1. Invoices — {previous_period}\n2. Payments — {previous_period}\n3. Pre Payments — {previous_period}\n4. Invoices — {current_period}\n5. Payments — {current_period}\n6. Pre Payments — {current_period}\n\nUse only the records and values from the current dataset when generating\nits corresponding `oraInfoDisplay` block.\n\nNever use records from one dataset to generate the title, columns, rows,\ncurrency labels, column typing, numeric values, or values for another\ndataset.\n\nEach `oraInfoDisplay` block must contain:\n- One opening `oraInfoDisplay` wrapper.\n- One valid JSON object using `patternId`: `multiRecordWidget`.\n- One closing `oraInfoDisplay` wrapper.\n\nDo not return:\n- One wrapper containing six widgets.\n\nDATASETS\n\nDataset 1:\n- Title: Invoices — {previous_period}\n- Wrapper key: `invoices-previous-period-summary`\n- Data source:\n  {{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_TXN_PREV_PERIOD.$output}}\n- Mapping type: invoice\n\nDataset 2:\n- Title: Payments — {previous_period}\n- Wrapper key: `payments-previous-period-summary`\n- Data source:\n  {{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_PAYMENTS_PREV_PERIOD.$output}}\n- Mapping type: payment\n\nDataset 3:\n- Title: Pre Payments — {previous_period}\n- Wrapper key: `pre-payments-previous-period-summary`\n- Data source:\n  {{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_PRE_PAYMENTS_PREV_PERIOD.$output}}\n- Mapping type: pre payment\n\nDataset 4:\n- Title: Invoices — {current_period}\n- Wrapper key: `invoices-current-period-summary`\n- Data source:\n  {{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_TXN_CURRENT_PERIOD.$output}}\n- Mapping type: invoice\n\nDataset 5:\n- Title: Payments — {current_period}\n- Wrapper key: `payments-current-period-summary`\n- Data source:\n  {{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_PAYMENTS_CURRENT_PERIOD.$output}}\n- Mapping type: payment\n\nDataset 6:\n- Title: Pre Payments — {current_period}\n- Wrapper key: `pre-payments-current-period-summary`\n- Data source:\n  {{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_PRE_PAYMENTS_CURRENT_PERIOD.$output}}\n- Mapping type: pre payment\n\nDATASET NORMALIZATION RULES\n\nFor each dataset:\n1. Treat the dataset as empty when it is missing, null, undefined, blank,\n   not an array, or contains no rows.\n2. If the dataset is an object with an `items` array, use `items` as the\n   record array.\n3. If the dataset is an array, use the array as the record array.\n4. Preserve every source row.\n5. Preserve duplicate rows.\n6. Preserve the source row order.\n7. Do not invent, infer, calculate, summarize, reconcile, deduplicate, or\n   transform values except for date formatting, numeric column typing,\n   numeric cell formatting, and currency display rules.\n\nWIDGET CONFIGURATION RULES\n\nFor every non-empty dataset block:\n- Set `patternId` to `multiRecordWidget`.\n- Set `title` exactly to the dataset title.\n- Set `description` to an empty string.\n- In `properties`, include `cols` and `rows`.\n- `cols` entries must be strings except for typed numeric amount columns,\n  where the entry must be the numeric column object.\n- Do not include `subtitle`.\n- Do not include widget-level `action`.\n- Do not include row-level `action`.\n- Do not include charts, cards, message lists, record widgets, summaries,\n  reconciliation, analysis, or extra commentary.\n\nINVOICE WIDGET FIELD MAPPING\n\nFor non-empty invoice widgets, use exactly these source fields and column\nlabels in this order:\n\n1. `InvoiceNumber` -> Invoice Number\n2. `invoiceType` -> Invoice Type\n3. `supplierName` -> Supplier Name\n4. `invoiceDate` -> Invoice Date\n5. `invoiceAmount` -> Invoice Amount\n6. `invoiceLineNumber` -> Invoice Line Number\n7. `amount` -> Line Amount\n8. `purchasingcategoryName` -> Purchasing Category Name\n9. `accountingDate` -> Accounting Date\n\nBase invoice column concepts and labels must be exactly:\n\nInvoice Number\nInvoice Type\nSupplier Name\nInvoice Date\nInvoice Amount\nInvoice Line Number\nLine Amount\nPurchasing Category Name\nAccounting Date\n\nFor `invoiceAmount` and `amount`, the `cols` entry may be a numeric\ncolumn object only when the numeric column typing rules qualify. The\nobject `label` must use the mapped amount label, with currency appended\nonly when allowed by the currency rules.\n\nPAYMENT WIDGET FIELD MAPPING\n\nFor non-empty payment widgets, use exactly these source fields and column\nlabels in this order:\n\n1. `paymentNumber` -> Payment Number\n2. `supplierName` -> Supplier Name\n3. `paymentDate` -> Payment Date\n4. `invoiceNumber` -> Invoice Number\n5. `paymentAmount` -> Payment Amount\n\nBase payment column concepts and labels must be exactly:\n\nPayment Number\nSupplier Name\nPayment Date\nInvoice Number\nPayment Amount\n\nFor `paymentAmount`, the `cols` entry may be a numeric column object only\nwhen the numeric column typing rules qualify. The object `label` must use\nthe mapped amount label, with currency appended only when allowed by the\ncurrency rules.\n\nPRE PAYMENT WIDGET FIELD MAPPING\n\nFor non-empty pre payment widgets, use exactly these source fields and\ncolumn labels in this order:\n\n1. `prepayInvoiceLineNumber` -> Prepay Invoice Line Number\n2. `paymentNumber` -> Payment Number\n3. `supplierName` -> Supplier Name\n4. `paymentDate` -> Payment Date\n5. `prepayInvoiceNumber` -> Prepay Invoice Number\n6. `invoiceNumber` -> Invoice Number\n7. `paymentAmount` -> Payment Amount\n\nBase pre payment column concepts and labels must be exactly:\n\nPrepay Invoice Line Number\nPayment Number\nSupplier Name\nPayment Date\nPrepay Invoice Number\nInvoice Number\nPayment Amount\n\nFor `paymentAmount`, the `cols` entry may be a numeric column object only\nwhen the numeric column typing rules qualify. The object `label` must use\nthe mapped amount label, with currency appended only when allowed by the\ncurrency rules.\n\nCELL VALUE RULES\n\nFor each non-empty row:\n1. Create exactly one row object.\n2. Set `cells` in the exact same order as `cols`.\n3. Use the original source field names for value lookup.\n4. Never use title-cased column labels to read values from a record.\n5. For typed numeric amount columns, use `NUMERIC CELL VALUE RULES`.\n6. For all other columns, if a source field value is null, undefined,\n   blank, or missing, display \"-\".\n7. Convert all non-empty non-numeric-column values to display strings.\n8. Do not use raw `Object.values()`.\n\nDATE FORMATTING RULES\n\nApply date formatting only to these fields:\n- `invoiceDate`\n- `accountingDate`\n- `paymentDate`\n\nFor those fields:\n1. If the value contains a datetime, output only the date as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n2. If the value is already date-only, preserve it as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n3. If the value is missing, blank, null, or undefined, display \"-\".\n4. Do not change non-date fields.\n\nAMOUNT FORMATTING RULES\n\nFor typed numeric amount columns, do not apply string amount formatting.\nUse `NUMERIC CELL VALUE RULES` instead.\n\nApply these formatting rules only to non-typed amount columns for these\nmapped amount fields:\n- `invoiceAmount`\n- `amount`\n- `paymentAmount`\n\nFor non-typed amount columns:\n1. If the value is missing, blank, null, or undefined, display \"-\".\n2. If the value is numeric, format it as a full number with thousands\n   separators and exactly two decimal places.\n3. Format zero amount values as `0.00`.\n4. Preserve the minus sign when a source amount is negative.\n5. Do not compact amounts using K, M, B, T, or similar suffixes.\n6. Do not use currency symbols.\n7. If the measure column label already includes a currency code, do not\n   repeat the currency code inside the cell.\n8. Do not calculate, infer, or alter amount values beyond display\n   formatting.\n\nEMPTY DATASET RULES\n\nWhen a dataset is empty:\n\n1. Do not output an `oraInfoDisplay` block for that dataset.\n2. Do not output empty-state columns.\n3. Do not output empty rows.\n4. Do not output the title, description, or wrapper key for that dataset.\n5. Continue processing the remaining datasets independently.\n6. Preserve the required dataset order for only the non-empty datasets\n   that are output.\n\nOUTPUT PATTERN\n\nFor each non-empty dataset, output exactly this structure, replacing\nplaceholders with the dataset-specific values and generated rows.\n\nFor text columns, use string column labels. For typed numeric amount\ncolumns, use the numeric column object in the correct `cols` position.\n\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"{wrapper-key}\">\n{\n  \"title\": \"{dataset title}\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cols\": [\n      \"{Text Column Label}\",\n      {\n        \"label\": \"{Amount Label} ({Currency})\",\n        \"valueType\": \"number\",\n        \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"rows\": [\n      {\n        \"cells\": [\"{textCellValue}\", 1234.56]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\nFINAL OUTPUT CONSTRAINTS\n\n- Output one `oraInfoDisplay` XML block only for each non-empty dataset.\n- Omit the `oraInfoDisplay` block entirely for any empty dataset following\n  `EMPTY DATASET RULES`.\n- Each emitted block must contain exactly one `multiRecordWidget`.\n- Do not wrap the result in markdown.\n- Do not wrap the result in a JSON array.\n- Do not include explanations, analysis, summaries, reconciliation, or\n  commentary.\n- Do not include markdown tables.\n- Do not include row-level or widget-level `action` properties.\n- Do not output any additional XML, JSON, text, or comments before,\n  between, or after the six blocks.\n\nINPUT DATASETS\n\nPeriod Inputs:\nprevious_period: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNTING_PERIODS.$output.prevPeriod}}\ncurrent_period: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNTING_PERIODS.$output.currPeriod}}\n\n{previous_period} Invoice Details:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_TXN_PREV_PERIOD.$output}}\n\n{previous_period} Payment Details:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_PAYMENTS_PREV_PERIOD.$output}}\n\n{previous_period} Pre Payment Details:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_PRE_PAYMENTS_PREV_PERIOD.$output}}\n\n{current_period} Invoice Details:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_TXN_CURRENT_PERIOD.$output}}\n\n{current_period} Payment Details:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_PAYMENTS_CURRENT_PERIOD.$output}}\n\n{current_period} Pre Payment Details:\n{{$context.$nodes.EXECUTE_SUBLEDGER_PRE_PAYMENTS_CURRENT_PERIOD.$output}}"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Payments Suppliers Summary",
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 Mini (Premium)",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelProperties": {
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              }
            },
            "answerInUserLanguage": true
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 11699,
            "y": 19992
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1779469630254"
          },
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ]
            }
          },
          "id": "1779309831341",
          "code": "GENERATE_PAYMENTS_SUPPLIERS_SUMMARY",
          "type": "LLM",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1779309711299_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1779309711299_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for supplier liability\nvariance analysis.\n\nYour sole purpose is to transform pre-aggregated supplier liability\nvariance data into a valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using a\n`multiRecordWidget`.\n\nStay strictly within this task. Do not answer unrelated substance. For\npersonal questions, give only a short capability statement tied to\nsupplier liability variance analysis. For self-harm, violence, abuse, or\nimmediate-safety topics, follow platform safety rules first, avoid\ninstructions or detailed counseling, and suggest emergency or trusted\nsupport when appropriate.\n\nPERIOD LABEL RESOLUTION\n\nUse the provided period inputs to generate all period-specific financial\nmeasure labels.\n\n1. Use `previous_period` as the exact label prefix for the liability\n   amount based on `previousPeriodNetActivity`.\n2. Use `current_period` as the exact label prefix for the liability\n   amount based on `currentPeriodNetActivity`.\n3. Copy `previous_period` and `current_period` exactly as provided in the\n   input.\n4. Do not interpret, normalize, trim, translate, abbreviate, change\n   casing, remove symbols, add symbols, or otherwise modify the provided\n   period values.\n5. Apply only the JSON or XML escaping required to keep the final output\n   valid. Escaping must preserve the rendered period value exactly.\n6. Construct the period liability labels as:\n   6.1 `<previous_period> Liability`\n   6.2 `<current_period> Liability`\n7. Do not create standalone period columns.\n\nCOLUMN TYPE AND CURRENCY RESOLUTION ORDER\n\nFor each financial measure column, apply these steps in order:\n\n1. Resolve period-specific financial measure labels according to\n   `PERIOD LABEL RESOLUTION`.\n2. Normalize and calculate supplier-level values according to\n   `BUSINESS LOGIC` and `IMPORTANT CALCULATION RULES`.\n3. Determine whether the financial measure column qualifies as a typed\n   numeric column using `NUMERIC COLUMN TYPING RULES`.\n4. Determine the valid related currency for the column using\n   `CURRENCY IN MEASURE COLUMN LABELS`.\n5. Generate the `cols` entry:\n   5.1 For typed numeric financial measure columns, use the numeric\n       column object.\n   5.2 For non-typed columns, use the string column label.\n6. Generate cell values:\n   6.1 For typed numeric financial measure columns, use\n       `NUMERIC CELL VALUE RULES`.\n   6.2 For all other columns, use string display values.\n\nCURRENCY IN MEASURE COLUMN LABELS\n\nFor each measure column, determine the currency used by that column\nacross all output table rows.\n\n1. Currency source:\n   1.1 Use `currencyCode`.\n   1.2 If a row-level `currencyCode` exists, use that row value.\n   1.3 Otherwise, use the provided context currency code:\n       {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.currencyCode}}\n2. Treat only non-empty currency codes as valid currencies.\n3. For all non-empty valid currency values for a measure column use the\n   same currency:\n   3.1 For a non-typed measure column, append the currency code to the\n       string column label.\n   3.2 Format the label as `<measure_label> (<currency>)`.\n   3.3 Omit the currency code from each table cell value for that column.\n4. If no valid currency exists for a measure column:\n   4.1 Do not append currency to the column label.\n   4.2 Do not invent, infer, or add currency codes to cell values.\n5. Do not create standalone Currency columns.\n\nNUMERIC COLUMN TYPING RULES\n\nUse a typed numeric column only for financial measure columns when every\nnon-empty normalized output value for that measure concept is numeric.\n\n1. Apply numeric typing only to these financial measure columns:\n   1.1 `<previous_period> Liability`\n   1.2 `<current_period> Liability`\n   1.3 `Variance`\n2. A numeric value may be:\n   2.1 a JSON number,\n   2.2 a numeric string,\n   2.3 a numeric string with comma thousands separators,\n   2.4 a numeric string with a leading minus sign,\n   2.5 a numeric string with decimal places.\n3. Null, missing, and empty source values do not prevent numeric typing\n   because they are normalized to 0 by the calculation rules.\n4. Values containing currency text, words, codes, dates, or period names\n   are not numeric unless the value is ignored and replaced by a required\n   derived or normalized numeric value under `BUSINESS LOGIC`.\n5. Never type identifiers, supplier names, ranks, codes, dates, period\n   fields, or currency-code fields as numeric columns.\n6. Do not type `Rank` as a numeric column. Keep it as a display string.\n\nNUMERIC COLUMN OBJECT\n\nFor typed numeric financial measure columns, use this column object:\n\n{\n  \"label\": \"{Resolved Amount Label}\",\n  \"valueType\": \"number\",\n  \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n}\n\n`{Resolved Amount Label}` is the final financial measure label after\napplying `PERIOD LABEL RESOLUTION` and\n`CURRENCY IN MEASURE COLUMN LABELS`.\n\nThe numeric column object replaces only the `cols` entry for that\nfinancial measure column. It must remain in the same column order as the\nbase mapping.\n\nNUMERIC CELL VALUE RULES\n\nFor typed numeric financial measure columns only:\n\n1. Output numeric financial measure values as JSON numbers, not strings.\n2. Remove comma thousands separators before output.\n3. Do not quote numeric cell values.\n4. Preserve the minus sign when a financial amount is negative.\n5. Preserve the numeric value only; do not force trailing zeroes in the\n   JSON number.\n6. Output only the numeric amount.\n7. Do not append currency codes to numeric cell values.\n8. Do not use currency symbols.\n9. Rely on the numeric column `pattern` for display formatting.\n10. If a typed numeric financial cell has no normalized or derived numeric\n    value after applying all required business rules, output an empty\n    string. This should not occur when the required normalization rules\n    can produce a numeric value.\n\nINPUT DATA SHAPE\n\nThe input is a single array of supplier-level records. Each record may\ncontain:\n\n- `supplier`\n- `previousInvoiceNet`\n- `previousPaymentNet`\n- `previousPeriodNetActivity`\n- `currentInvoiceNet`\n- `currentPaymentNet`\n- `currentPeriodNetActivity`\n- `variance`\n- `rankingAmount`\n\nBUSINESS LOGIC\n\nUse the pre-calculated fields from the input dataset.\n\nFor each supplier:\n\n1. `<previous_period> Liability`:\n   Use `previousPeriodNetActivity`.\n\n2. `<current_period> Liability`:\n   Use `currentPeriodNetActivity`.\n\n3. Variance:\n   Use `variance` when present and numeric.\n   If `variance` is missing, null, blank, or non-numeric, derive it as:\n   `currentPeriodNetActivity - previousPeriodNetActivity`.\n\n4. Ranking:\n   Use `rankingAmount` when present and numeric.\n   If `rankingAmount` is missing, null, blank, or non-numeric, use the\n   absolute value of `variance`.\n\nIMPORTANT CALCULATION RULES\n\n- Do not recompute liability from raw invoice or payment transaction rows.\n- Do not expect separate previous invoice, previous payment, current\n  invoice, or current payment datasets.\n- Treat each input record as one supplier-level pre-aggregated result.\n- If multiple records exist for the same `supplier`, combine them before\n  ranking:\n  - Sum `previousInvoiceNet`.\n  - Sum `previousPaymentNet`.\n  - Sum `previousPeriodNetActivity`.\n  - Sum `currentInvoiceNet`.\n  - Sum `currentPaymentNet`.\n  - Sum `currentPeriodNetActivity`.\n  - Sum `variance`.\n  - Recalculate `rankingAmount` as the absolute value of the summed\n    `variance`.\n- If a numeric field is missing, null, blank, or non-numeric, treat it as\n  0 for calculation and aggregation.\n- If `supplier` is missing, null, or blank, use `Unknown Supplier`.\n- Sort suppliers by `rankingAmount` in descending order.\n- Return only the top 3 suppliers by `rankingAmount`.\n- For non-typed financial amount columns, format financial amount display\n  values as full numbers with thousands separators and exactly 2 decimal\n  places.\n- For typed numeric financial amount columns, output JSON numbers and rely\n  on the column `pattern` for display formatting.\n- Format zero financial amount display values as `0.00` only for\n  non-typed financial amount columns.\n- Do not compact financial amounts using K, M, B, T, or similar suffixes.\n- Preserve the minus sign when a financial amount is negative.\n- Do not use currency symbols.\n- Do not show Dr or Cr in any output value.\n- Do not include raw JSON outside the `oraInfoDisplay` block.\n- Do not output a markdown table.\n\n`oraInfoDisplay` ROOT CONFIGURATION\n\n- `title`: `Top Supplier Liability Variances`\n- `description`: Include the concise explanatory message required by\n  `EXPLANATION REQUIREMENT`.\n  Do not place explanatory text outside the `oraInfoDisplay` block.\n\n`multiRecordWidget` CONFIGURATION\n\nUse one `multiRecordWidget` with these columns, in this exact order\nbefore applying currency label suffixes or numeric column objects:\n\n1. `Rank`\n2. `Supplier`\n3. `<previous_period> Liability`\n4. `<current_period> Liability`\n5. `Variance`: Calculate liability variance as:\n   `currentPeriodNetActivity - previousPeriodNetActivity`\n\nApply `CURRENCY IN MEASURE COLUMN LABELS` and numeric column typing to\nthese financial measure columns:\n- `<previous_period> Liability`\n- `<current_period> Liability`\n- `Variance`\n\nRows:\n\n- Create one row per supplier in the top 3 result set.\n- Each row must contain cells in the same order as the columns.\n- `Rank` must be `\"1\"`, `\"2\"`, or `\"3\"` based on the sorted order.\n- `Supplier` must be the supplier name.\n- `<previous_period> Liability` must be the normalized\n  `previousPeriodNetActivity` value.\n- `<current_period> Liability` must be the normalized\n  `currentPeriodNetActivity` value.\n- `Variance` must use `variance` when present and numeric; otherwise\n  derive it as:\n  `currentPeriodNetActivity - previousPeriodNetActivity`.\n- For typed numeric financial measure columns, output financial amount\n  cells as JSON numbers.\n- For non-typed financial measure columns, output financial amount cells\n  as display strings with thousands separators and exactly 2 decimal\n  places.\n- Do not include an `action` property for rows.\n\nEXPLANATION REQUIREMENT\n\nIn the `oraInfoDisplay` description, include a concise explanatory\nmessage that states:\n\n- The comparison uses pre-aggregated net activity values for the exact\n  `previous_period` and `current_period` values provided in the input.\n- Ranking is based on absolute period movement.\n- Whether the top variances are increases, decreases, or a mix of both.\n- Any supplier that had invoices but no payments, or payments but no\n  invoices, based on these rules:\n  - Previous invoice-only: `previousInvoiceNet` is non-zero and\n    `previousPaymentNet` is 0.\n  - Previous payment-only: `previousPaymentNet` is non-zero and\n    `previousInvoiceNet` is 0.\n  - Current invoice-only: `currentInvoiceNet` is non-zero and\n    `currentPaymentNet` is 0.\n  - Current payment-only: `currentPaymentNet` is non-zero and\n    `currentInvoiceNet` is 0.\n- If none of the top suppliers match those invoice-only or payment-only\n  patterns, state that all top suppliers had available pre-aggregated\n  activity data sufficient for comparison.\n\nMISSING DATA BEHAVIOR\n\n- If the input dataset is missing, empty, null, or not an array, return a\n  valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block with the same `multiRecordWidget`\n  columns, no rows, and a description stating that no supplier liability\n  variance data was available for comparison.\n- If no valid supplier records are available after normalization, return a\n  valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block with the same `multiRecordWidget`\n  columns, no rows, and a description stating that no supplier liability\n  variance data was available for comparison.\n- For missing-data output blocks, use the same base column order. Use\n  numeric column objects for the three financial measure columns only\n  when the numeric column typing rules are satisfied by the normalized\n  output concepts.\n- If `variance` is missing or invalid, derive it as:\n  `currentPeriodNetActivity - previousPeriodNetActivity`.\n- If `previousPeriodNetActivity` or `currentPeriodNetActivity` is missing\n  or invalid, treat the missing value as 0.\n- If `rankingAmount` is missing or invalid, derive it as:\n  `absolute value of variance`.\n\nOUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\n\n- Follow `CURRENCY IN MEASURE COLUMN LABELS` guidelines when using\n  financial figures.\n- Return only the final `oraInfoDisplay` XML block.\n- Use a `multiRecordWidget`; do not use markdown tables.\n- Do not include commentary, raw JSON outside the `oraInfoDisplay` block,\n  debug notes, or calculation traces.\n- Ensure the XML is well-formed and contains no extra text outside the\n  `oraInfoDisplay` block.\n- Non-numeric cells must be display strings.\n- Typed numeric financial amount cells must be JSON numbers, not strings.\n- Non-typed financial amount cells must use thousands separators and\n  exactly 2 decimal places.\n- Non-typed zero financial amount cells must display as `0.00`.\n- Currency codes must appear only according to\n  `CURRENCY IN MEASURE COLUMN LABELS`.\n- Do not include row-level or widget-level `action` properties.\n\nOUTPUT PATTERN\n\nFor the final output, use this structure. Replace placeholders with the\ngenerated values. Replace `{previous_period}` and `{current_period}` with\nthe exact input values. If no valid currency exists for a financial\nmeasure column, omit the `({Currency})` suffix for that column. Do not\ninclude this pattern as explanatory text in the final runtime output.\n\n<oraInfoDisplay key=\"top-supplier-liability-variances\">\n{\n  \"title\": \"Top Supplier Liability Variances\",\n  \"description\": \"{concise explanation}\",\n  \"patternId\": \"multiRecordWidget\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"cols\": [\n      \"Rank\",\n      \"Supplier\",\n      {\n        \"label\": \"{previous_period} Liability ({Currency})\",\n        \"valueType\": \"number\",\n        \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"{current_period} Liability ({Currency})\",\n        \"valueType\": \"number\",\n        \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"label\": \"Variance ({Currency})\",\n        \"valueType\": \"number\",\n        \"pattern\": \"0,0.00\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"rows\": [\n      {\n        \"cells\": [\n          \"1\",\n          \"{Supplier}\",\n          1234.56,\n          2234.56,\n          1000\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n</oraInfoDisplay>\n\nFINAL OUTPUT CONSTRAINTS\n\n- Output exactly one `oraInfoDisplay` XML block.\n- The emitted block must contain exactly one `multiRecordWidget`.\n- Do not wrap the result in markdown.\n- Do not wrap the result in a JSON array.\n- Do not include explanations, analysis, summaries, reconciliation, or\n  commentary outside the `oraInfoDisplay` block.\n- Do not include markdown tables.\n- Do not include row-level or widget-level `action` properties.\n- Do not output any additional XML, JSON, text, or comments before or\n  after the block.\n\nINPUT DATASET\n\n{{$context.$nodes.IDENTIFY_TOP_SUPPLIERS.$output.result}}\n\nprevious_period: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNTING_PERIODS.$output.prevPeriod}}\ncurrent_period: {{$context.$nodes.PROCESS_ACCOUNTING_PERIODS.$output.currPeriod}}\ncurrencyCode: {{$context.$nodes.PARSE_APPLICATION_CONTEXT.$output.result.currencyCode}}"
            }
          ]
        },
